{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it — he mocks</b>, from the root לעג and קלס, and like it לקלס אתנן." "<b>And he heaps dust</b> — as though he heaped all the dust of the earth; or it is a figure of speech: he heaps dust and takes every fortress."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The comment glosses ויתקלס in the verse; the subject (the Chaldean) is implied."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:07.658574014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}